From 27c4fcb0161e80c17cdc555f6e94abbd5745edbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:37:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Guest networks: paths to the main network the admin opts
 into; Rule Status shows held paths

- Reach these main-network devices (per isolated guest network, off by default): guests may open
  connections to the main-network devices the admin ticks (DHCP reservations only, never AiMesh nodes,
  never the router); the devices only answer. The guest isolation chains stay deny-only; the accept
  lives in its own chain after Gatekeeper and the rules engine. Re-applied when reservations change.
- Device discovery with the main network (per network, off by default): mDNS between the main network
  and that network only, never between two guest networks, limited to the service types picked
  (printing, AirPlay, Google Cast, HomeKit / Matter, Spotify / Sonos, own entries). The router's own
  names are not announced there, and a guest device cannot take over a main-network name or withdraw a
  main-network service. The avahi config reader takes lines up to 4 KB.
- Firewall > Zones switch (off by default): an Accept zone policy from the main network (or a network
  linked to it) into an isolated guest network opens that path one way; never guest to guest.
- Rule Status 1.16: a zone policy that guest isolation holds is "Held" (amber), not failed; new rows
  for chosen devices, discovery and the reverse direction of an opened path. The dashboard, the
  diagnostics bundle and the AI Advisor describe the held state.
- services.c also carries the IPv6 gates of the previous commit and the AP Isolation calls of the next;
  web.c also the AiMesh MLO mark and the AP Isolation keys; defaults.c / init.c also those keys and the
  /56 default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
